{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2043 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "4291e5e641436f73b991a0d374d545b25d6dd1467710f446b01f86edf1e28a5e" :edb/db-before-t 2042 :edb/db-after-t 2043 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535355 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:41:50.193Z" 13194139535355 true] [17592186133689 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345415 13194139535355 true] [17592186133788 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345408 13194139535355 true] [17592186134472 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535355 true] [17592186134472 1100 "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨ \\cdot, \\cdot ⟩$ over $C$.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $⟨a, 0⟩ = 0$ for any $a ∈ C^{n}$\n2. $2⟨a, b⟩ = ⟨a,-2b⟩$ for any $a, b ∈ C^{n}$\n3. $⟨a, b⟩ ∈ R$ for any $a, b ∈ C^{n}$" 13194139535355 false] [17592186134472 1100 "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,0⟩=0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $2⟨a,b⟩=⟨a,-2b⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" 13194139535355 true] [17592186134472 1145 "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the antilinearity in the second argument we have that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,0⟩ & =⟨a,0\\cdot 0⟩=\\overset{―}{0}⟨a,0⟩=0⟨a,0⟩=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,-2b⟩=\\overset{―}{(-2)}⟨a,b⟩=-2⟨a,b⟩\\ne 2⟨a,b⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number, in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345408 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345409 13194139535355 true] [17592186345408 1089 "q-97186" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345408 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535355 true] [17592186345408 1100 "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,(3+2\\text{i})b+c⟩$ if  \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=2\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨c,a⟩=1+\\text{i}.$" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345408 1113 #uuid "88b94b51-b062-5eeb-8efa-fd6575e3a7d9" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345408 1145 "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,(3+2\\text{i})b+c⟩ & =⟨a,(3+2\\text{i})b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(\\overset{―}{3+2\\text{i}})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(3-2\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-2\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ & =(3-2\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨c,a⟩:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-2\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩} & =(3-2\\text{i})\\cdot \\overset{―}{2\\text{i}}+\\overset{―}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =(3-2\\text{i})\\cdot (-2\\text{i})+(1-\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-6\\text{i}+4{\\text{i}}^{2}+1-\\text{i} \\\\  & =-6\\text{i}+4(-1)+1-\\text{i} \\\\  & =-3-7\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345410 13194139535355 true] [17592186345409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345411 13194139535355 true] [17592186345409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345412 13194139535355 true] [17592186345409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345413 13194139535355 true] [17592186345409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345414 13194139535355 true] [17592186345409 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535355 true] [17592186345409 1041 "selection" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345409 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345411 13194139535355 true] [17592186345409 1110 #uuid "4817ab3d-9707-52d0-81de-039b292b0f9f" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345410 1034 "-2-\\text{i}" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345410 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535355 true] [17592186345410 1111 #uuid "b9d35b78-ec2b-5d53-94e5-6684eca0c7ff" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345411 1034 "-3-7\\text{i}" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345411 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535355 true] [17592186345411 1111 #uuid "6aaacb3d-e06d-56ec-8f8f-9acc52471306" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345412 1034 "-\\text{i}" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345412 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535355 true] [17592186345412 1111 #uuid "71661365-fa53-5f69-8666-c63cfbc735ca" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345413 1034 "5" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345413 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535355 true] [17592186345413 1111 #uuid "8115b771-4e3e-54fc-b500-fee828c7e802" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345414 1034 "-4\\text{i}" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535355 true] [17592186345414 1111 #uuid "287e35e0-fe90-52c7-bf4f-7ac56737b8c8" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345415 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345416 13194139535355 true] [17592186345415 1089 "q-97264" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345415 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535355 true] [17592186345415 1100 "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n- $⟨a,a⟩>0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345415 1113 #uuid "7bec15a8-acbd-5153-8a77-8304f45069a3" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345415 1145 "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\overset{―}{(\\overset{―}{\\alpha })}⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $a=0$ then $⟨a,a⟩=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345417 13194139535355 true] [17592186345416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345418 13194139535355 true] [17592186345416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345419 13194139535355 true] [17592186345416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345420 13194139535355 true] [17592186345416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345421 13194139535355 true] [17592186345416 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535355 true] [17592186345416 1041 "selection" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345416 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345421 13194139535355 true] [17592186345416 1110 #uuid "747ac466-10cb-55a4-8118-04fb2e7ddb8d" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345417 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535355 true] [17592186345417 1111 #uuid "d6a7b9bb-7fc4-545f-807f-9c546328ec61" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345418 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535355 true] [17592186345418 1111 #uuid "11261b75-1c15-5011-88c7-d1867147fb68" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345419 1034 "I only" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345419 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535355 true] [17592186345419 1111 #uuid "e7910e0e-f403-52a0-b630-fad878c73967" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345420 1034 "III only" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345420 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535355 true] [17592186345420 1111 #uuid "01370c31-0294-5c8a-8239-6098e39882d9" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345421 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535355 true] [17592186345421 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535355 true] [17592186345421 1111 #uuid "66b74a16-a25a-55a3-b76b-7a45689c8aec" 13194139535355 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-97186" 17592186345408 "q-97186/selection" 17592186345409 "q-97186/selection/71f893fe3e6205a25234d999b74bc7d00fb0973b3acd06d3074a7b14e4914301" 17592186345410 "q-97186/selection/a61e54cbc4fe752895ee7d0648c2ab327d52d00df87e6cc86875833915075354" 17592186345411 "q-97186/selection/c6a9189afe903fc860b7e81